## Use Case for eu-ehds:DataPermit
Description: This example illustrates the formal legal authorisation required for post-market Drug Safety Monitoring, which is a high-priority 
secondary use category under the EHDS. It centers on a use case where a National Medicines Agency (acting as the dpv:LegalEntity acting as the 
dpv:Recipient) must investigate an unexpected side effect linked to a specific cardiovascular medication by analysing health data across multiple 
regions. Because this involves processing sensitive clinical records for a regulatory purpose rather than individual patient care, it requires a 
eu-ehds:DataPermit issued by a Health Data Access Body (HDAB) under EHDS Article 68. The data permit acts as the formal dpv:OrganisationalMeasure
providing the Official Authority to access the data. It identifies the Medicines Agency as the authorised recipient and strictly limits the 
processing to sector-health:PublicHealthMonitoring activities within the health sector. Modeling this as a eu-ehds:DataPermit, the framework 
ensures the data remains within a Secure Processing Environment (SPE) and is used only for the time-bound duration of the safety investigation. 
The metadata includes the authorisation of the Medicines Agency, the specific legal basis under GDPR Art. 6(1)(e) of dpv:OfficialAuthorityOfController, 
and the requirement for a protected environment, providing a machine-readable guarantee that the agency’s access is strictly limited to the 
necessary window for ensuring public safety.

